    "body": "Diagnosis (phase 1, read only, no build).\n\n## Failure text\n\nThe step log is in the run artifact `gate-logs-post-merge-44780029308-1`, file `494-app_suites_example_catalog.log`:\n\n```\nthread 'contract::two_broken_cases_report_both_names_and_times' panicked at crates/app/tests/example_catalog/contract.rs:59:13:\nmissing time for 2d/contour-tabs:\nthread '<unnamed>' (1052937) panicked at crates/app/tests/example_catalog/support.rs:68:5:\n2d/contour-tabs: missing model/\ncatalog 2d/contour-tabs regenerates\nthread '<unnamed>' (1052938) panicked at crates/app/tests/example_catalog/support.rs:68:5:\n2d/first-part: missing model/\n elapsed=0.000s budget=60.000s\ncatalog 2d/first-part regenerates elapsed=0.001s budget=60.000s\n```\n\n## Cause\n\nThe scratch-root override works. The inner run fails fast on the empty root, in 0.000 s (`missing model/`). The issue title guess is not correct.\n\nThe fault is interleaved stderr output in the inner run:\n\n- The inner run starts the two broken cases in parallel (no `--test-threads`).\n- `within` writes its timing line with `writeln!(std::io::stderr(), ...)` (`support.rs:289-294`). Stderr has no buffer, so each format piece is a separate write call.\n- The default panic hook of the other case thread writes to the raw stderr. It does not take the `Stderr` lock. Its text got in between `catalog 2d/contour-tabs regenerates` and ` elapsed=`.\n- The assert at `contract.rs:58-62` looks for the contiguous text `catalog {case} {action} elapsed=`. It does not find it.\n\nThis is a race. It occurs more on a loaded Linux runner (16 lanes) than on Windows. It is not related to the merges between the green and the red run. The 59 s is the time of the full outer binary (the `turning/cone-thread` case takes 29 s). It is not the time of the contract test.\n\n## Repair (phase 2)\n\n1. `support.rs` `within`: make the full timing line into one `String` first, then write it with one `write_all` on the locked stderr. A pipe write of less than `PIPE_BUF` bytes is atomic, so no other text can split the line.\n2. `contract.rs`: give the inner run `--test-threads=1`. Then the two broken cases run one after the other and the inner output is deterministic. The assert does not change: it still requires the two `... FAILED` names and the two `elapsed=` lines.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
