    "body": "The post-merge gate on the current tip `ee91ac3e5` is green (run 44785615012, 17:40-17:53Z, this suite ok). That does not prove the fault gone: the code of this suite is the same in `768fe23f0` and `ee91ac3e5`. The red was likely the two inner cases racing, so a green alone is not a close.\n\nDraft PR #3044 (branch `issue/3043-catalog-contract-test`, head `c1ba0fe3f`) holds the fix: the timing line is written once, and the test runs its two cases in order. Its commit closes this issue on merge. Correction to my first note here: the cause is the split write and the parallel run, not the catalog-root override.\n",
